FAULT_DESCRIPTION:
The linter found that the multi-line string `jsonencode({
    id       = "__credential_id__"
    secret   = "__credential_secret__"
    region   = "test-region"
    username = "static-user"
  })` appears twice in the file (lines 60-65 and 372-375). The goconst linter enforces the DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself) principle by requiring repeated string literals to be extracted as constants. This improves maintainability by ensuring that if the string needs to be changed, it only needs to be updated in one place. The linter threshold is set to flag strings that appear 2 or more times.
